<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		VFE Medieval 2. This folder only loads when VFE Medieval 2 is active (see loadFolders.xml).
		  - The travelling merchant guild also fields Det's Brawnum and Boglegs (0.1 each, each MayRequire'd).
		  - The warbow can also be made at a crafting spot (upstream: smithies only).
		  - The heavy plate helmet stops inheriting the machining table from its parent, so it is smithy-only.
		  - The palisade no longer holds up roofs (upstream: holdsRoof true).
		The last three are VFE Medieval 2 tweaks with no partner mod; the user filed the block under integrations as a whole.
		Verified against VFE Medieval 2 1.6: all four targets exist with the upstream values noted, and neither xenotype is
		already listed. Progression: Attire also appends Medieval Overhaul's anvil to the helmet's recipeUsers, which stacks.
		Split by category into the MMMM Integrations sub-mods: this copy holds only the Other ops (everything else (thoughts, sanity, meditation focus, hediffs, animals, plants)).
	-->
	<!--
		With VFE Furniture: VFE Medieval 2's training dummy counts as VFE's "strength play" recreation instead of vanilla
		dexterity gaming, in the building, its play job and its joy giver. Verified all three upstream values are
		Gaming_Dexterity and VFE_StrengthPlay exists. Rimbody's melee-exercise tag on the same job is unaffected.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationSequence">
		<operations>
			<li Class="PatchOperationSequence" MayRequire="VanillaExpanded.VFECore">
				<operations>
					<li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
						<xpath>Defs/JobDef[defName="VFEM2_Play_TrainingDummy"]/joyKind</xpath>
						<value>
							<joyKind>VFE_StrengthPlay</joyKind>
						</value>
					</li>
					<li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
						<xpath>Defs/JoyGiverDef[defName="VFEM2_Play_TrainingDummy"]/joyKind</xpath>
						<value>
							<joyKind>VFE_StrengthPlay</joyKind>
						</value>
					</li>
				</operations>
			</li>
		</operations>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
